    "title": "Dog owner in deadly Chatham County attack charged with involuntary manslaughter: Sheriff - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matthew Sockol ,\n12 hours ago APEX, N.C. (WNCN) — The owner of the dogs involved in a deadly attack on a woman in Chatham County last week is facing a felony charge, deputies said Wednesday. According to the Chatham County Sheriff’s Office, 85-year-old Betty Alston was found dead outside of a home in the 200 block of Alston Road near Apex just before 11 a.m. on May 19. A family member told deputies that he chased away three dogs near her body in the yard. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 6",
